{
  "key": "E014",
  "title": "Robustness of lag-aware control to loop-model error, and a model-free ablation",
  "research_question": "Does lag-aware joint control stay safe when its model of the coolant loop's mass and the plant's ramp limit is wrong by 4x, and does it need a loop model at all?",
  "hypothesis": "Conditions: the 6 slow-loop conditions of E011 at 40 C ambient (3 cold-plate states x 2 loops), S6 profile, measured leakage slope and clock sensitivity. H1 (replication): joint_lag with the exact loop model records zero chip-seconds above 80 C in all 6. H2 (robust to model error): joint_lag records zero chip-seconds above 80 C in all 6 conditions with each of the four wrong models (loop mass x0.25 and x4, ramp x0.25 and x4). H3 (no model needed for safety): joint_meas records at most 10 chip-seconds above 80 C (seed mean) in each of the 6 conditions and never throttles. H4 (no model needed for cost): joint_meas's energy per successful task is within +/-1% of joint_lag's (95% CI of joint_meas / joint_lag - 1 inside +/-1%) and its late tasks within 1 per run, in all 6. H5 (model error costs little): for each wrong model, joint_lag's energy per successful task is within +/-1% of the exact-model joint_lag's (95% CI) in all 6 conditions.",
  "null_hypothesis": "Lag-aware control's safety depends on an accurate loop model.",
  "independent_variables": [
    "cold-plate state (3)",
    "loop (2)",
    "loop-model error (5, joint_lag)",
    "policy (joint_lag, joint_meas)"
  ],
  "dependent_variables": [
    "chip_s_over_target",
    "chip_s_throttled",
    "peak_T_j_C",
    "slo_violations",
    "success_rate",
    "E_per_success_kJ"
  ],
  "controlled_variables": [
    "S6 load profile",
    "seeds 0-4",
    "warm start",
    "leakage matched to the measured slope (kappa 0.02)",
    "clock sensitivity from M001",
    "twin knows the true cold-plate state and the loop's mass and ramp limit"
  ],
  "baseline": "joint_lag with the exact loop model within each condition",
  "configuration": "As E011 at 40 C ambient on both slow loops. True loops {'dyn40': (40.0, 1.0), 'dyn150': (150.0, 0.25)} (mass kg, ramp K/min); model errors {'exact': (1.0, 1.0), 'mass_x0.25': (0.25, 1.0), 'mass_x4': (4.0, 1.0), 'ramp_x0.25': (1.0, 0.25), 'ramp_x4': (1.0, 4.0)} (factors on mass, ramp) applied to the controller's model only.",
  "evaluation_criteria": "Thermal outcomes and late tasks as seed means over 5 seeds; energy as paired relative differences with 95% t-CI (joint_meas and wrong-model joint_lag paired seed by seed with exact-model joint_lag in the same condition).",
  "known_limitations": "Everything in E011's limitations, including the single well-mixed tank in both simulator and controller: a model-structure error (stratification, transport delay) is not tested. Model errors are applied one at a time. 40 C ambient only.",
  "disclosure": "Known when written: E011 and E011B results; E012 and E013 were running or queued and none of their results had been looked at. joint_meas was exercised only by unit tests (one 30-minute run of the default configuration and one decision on a constructed observation). No E014 cell was run before registration.",
